usage: last30days.py [-h] [--research-only]
                     [--emit {compact,json,context,md,html,brief}]
                     [--register {default,exec,dev,creator,eli5}]
                     [--json-profile {agent,raw}] [--search SEARCH] [--quick]
                     [--deep] [--verify-freshness | --no-verify-freshness]
                     [--drill TARGET] [--discover [DOMAIN]]
                     [--discover-shallow] [--nominate-only] [--judgments PATH]
                     [--finalize] [--angles PATH] [--debug] [--mock]
                     [--diagnose] [--preflight] [--welcome]
                     [--no-browser-cookies] [--save-dir SAVE_DIR]
                     [--resolve-save-dir] [--corpus DIR] [--corpus-all-time]
                     [--output OUTPUT] [--synthesis-file SYNTHESIS_FILE]
                     [--cached-report] [--publish-html] [--publish]
                     [--publish-password PUBLISH_PASSWORD] [--store]
                     [--x-handle X_HANDLE] [--x-related X_RELATED]
                     [--official-site DOMAIN] [--no-x-handle REASON]
                     [--x-posts PATH]
                     [--web-backend {auto,brave,exa,serper,parallel,parallel-mcp,keyless,none}]
                     [--perplexity-search-type {web,fast}] [--deep-research]
                     [--hiring-signals] [--plan PLAN]
                     [--save-suffix SAVE_SUFFIX] [--subreddits SUBREDDITS]
                     [--dedicated-subreddits DEDICATED_SUBREDDITS]
                     [--devto-tags DEVTO_TAGS]
                     [--tiktok-hashtags TIKTOK_HASHTAGS]
                     [--tiktok-creators TIKTOK_CREATORS]
                     [--ig-creators IG_CREATORS] [--days LOOKBACK_DAYS]
                     [--as-of AS_OF_DATE] [--max-results MAX_RESULTS]
                     [--max-per-source MAX_PER_SOURCE]
                     [--max-source-fetches MAX_SOURCE_FETCHES]
                     [--auto-resolve] [--github-user GITHUB_USER]
                     [--github-repo GITHUB_REPO]
                     [--trustpilot-domain TRUSTPILOT_DOMAIN]
                     [--amazon-query AMAZON_QUERY]
                     [--meta-ads-page META_ADS_PAGE]
                     [--telegram-sources TELEGRAM_SOURCES] [--competitors [N]]
                     [--competitors-list COMPETITORS_LIST]
                     [--polymarket-keywords POLYMARKET_KEYWORDS]
                     [--competitors-plan COMPETITORS_PLAN]
                     [topic ...]

Research a topic across live social, market, and grounded web sources.

positional arguments:
  topic                 Research topic

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --research-only       Treat the topic as research text, never as an
                        administrative command
  --emit {compact,json,context,md,html,brief}
  --register {default,exec,dev,creator,eli5}
                        Audience synthesis preset for the standard brief
                        (default, exec, dev, creator, eli5)
  --json-profile {agent,raw}
                        JSON export profile for --emit=json (default: agent)
  --search SEARCH       Comma-separated source list
  --quick               Lower-latency retrieval profile
  --deep                Higher-recall retrieval profile
  --verify-freshness    Re-check source-grounded claims after research, or
                        verify the cached report when no topic is supplied
  --no-verify-freshness
                        Disable freshness verification configured by
                        LAST30DAYS_VERIFY_FRESHNESS
  --drill TARGET        Deep follow-up on a cluster from the fresh last-
                        report.json cache
  --discover [DOMAIN]   Sweep river listings and rank the topics accelerating
                        in a domain; each survivor gets a full research pass.
                        Bare --discover (no domain) runs global trending
                        across every feed's hot list
  --discover-shallow    Skip the per-topic research pass during --discover:
                        rank on listing evidence only (faster, thinner; the
                        confidence floor still applies)
  --nominate-only       Leg 1 of the host-judged discovery protocol: sweep,
                        write the nominations bundle for host judgment, and
                        stop (no judging, no enrichment). Requires --discover
  --judgments PATH      Leg 2 of the discovery protocol: resume from the
                        nominations bundle, applying the host judgments file
                        at PATH. Requires --discover
  --finalize            Leg 3 of the discovery protocol: apply host angles,
                        render the final discovery brief, and record the topic
                        queue. Requires --discover
  --angles PATH         Optional host angles file for --discover --finalize
                        (omitting it ships the brief without angle lines)
  --debug               Enable HTTP debug logging
  --mock                Use mock retrieval fixtures
  --diagnose            Print provider and source availability
  --preflight           Print a safe human-readable permission preflight
  --welcome             Print the first-run welcome text (engine-owned; relay
                        verbatim)
  --no-browser-cookies  Disable browser-cookie extraction even when
                        FROM_BROWSER is configured
  --save-dir SAVE_DIR   Optional directory for saving the rendered output
  --resolve-save-dir    Print the skill save directory from flags/config, then
                        exit without research
  --corpus DIR          Add a local .md/.txt/.pdf directory as a private
                        ranked source (repeatable)
  --corpus-all-time     Include matching corpus files older than the research
                        window
  --output OUTPUT       Optional exact file path for saving the rendered
                        output
  --synthesis-file SYNTHESIS_FILE
                        Markdown synthesis to embed in --emit=html output
  --cached-report       Render --emit=html --synthesis-file from cached
                        research only, without replaying temporary plans
  --publish-html        Publish --emit=html output to ht-ml.app (explicit opt-
                        in; public by default)
  --publish             With 'library feed', publish the HTML index and briefs
                        (explicit opt-in; public by default); feed.xml remains
                        local
  --publish-password PUBLISH_PASSWORD
                        Optional shared password for --publish-html or
                        'library feed --publish'; prefer
                        LAST30DAYS_PUBLISH_PASSWORD to avoid exposing secrets
                        in process lists
  --store               Persist ranked findings to the SQLite research store
  --x-handle X_HANDLE   X handle for targeted supplemental search
  --x-related X_RELATED
                        Comma-separated related X handles (searched with lower
                        weight)
  --official-site DOMAIN
                        The topic's own website (e.g., typesafe.ai). The
                        engine reads the X and GitHub accounts the homepage
                        links and uses them when --x-handle / --github-user
                        are not set. Keyless.
  --no-x-handle REASON  Record that the topic has no resolvable X account, and
                        why (e.g., "official site links no X account; x.com-
                        filtered search found none"). Satisfies the agent-
                        hosted X handle decision check without --x-handle.
  --x-posts PATH        Path to a last30days-x-posts/1 JSON envelope of posts
                        the hosting model fetched through its X connector;
                        replaces the engine's X fetch for this run. A file
                        path only (never inline JSON); on a comparison run use
                        the per-entity x_posts field of --competitors-plan.
  --web-backend {auto,brave,exa,serper,parallel,parallel-mcp,keyless,none}
                        Web search backend (default: auto; parallel-mcp
                        explicitly opts into the anonymous hosted MCP; keyless
                        forces the zero-key floor)
  --perplexity-search-type {web,fast}
                        Search backend for direct Perplexity Search API and
                        Agent web_search; overrides
                        LAST30DAYS_PERPLEXITY_SEARCH_TYPE. Does not enable the
                        paid source or select an Agent preset.
  --deep-research       Use at most one Perplexity Deep Research run. Direct
                        PERPLEXITY_API_KEY uses the Agent API background path;
                        OPENROUTER_API_KEY keeps the synchronous Sonar
                        fallback; cannot be combined with competitor or vs-
                        mode.
  --hiring-signals      Analyze public jobs/careers postings as evidence-
                        backed company focus signals.
  --plan PLAN           JSON query plan (skips internal LLM planner). Can be a
                        JSON string or a file path.
  --save-suffix SAVE_SUFFIX
                        Suffix for saved output filename (e.g., 'gemini' →
                        kanye-west-raw-gemini.md)
  --subreddits SUBREDDITS
                        Comma-separated broad/category subreddit names to
                        search (e.g., SaaS,Entrepreneur)
  --dedicated-subreddits DEDICATED_SUBREDDITS
                        Comma-separated entity-home subreddit names (e.g.,
                        Kanye,WestSubEver). Pulled in full (top+hot+new) and
                        exempt from the relevance floor since the whole sub is
                        the topic.
  --devto-tags DEVTO_TAGS
                        Comma-separated dev.to tags, lowercase alphanumeric
                        (e.g., claudecode,ai)
  --tiktok-hashtags TIKTOK_HASHTAGS
                        Comma-separated TikTok hashtags without # (e.g.,
                        tella,screenrecording)
  --tiktok-creators TIKTOK_CREATORS
                        Comma-separated TikTok creator handles (e.g.,
                        TellaHQ,taborplace)
  --ig-creators IG_CREATORS
                        Comma-separated Instagram creator handles (e.g.,
                        tella.tv,laborstories)
  --days LOOKBACK_DAYS, --lookback-days LOOKBACK_DAYS
                        Number of days to look back for research (default: 30,
                        watchlist uses 90)
  --as-of AS_OF_DATE    End date for the lookback window in YYYY-MM-DD format.
                        When set, --days looks back from this date instead of
                        today.
  --max-results MAX_RESULTS
                        Override the final ranked-pool cap
                        (pool_limit/rerank_limit) from the depth profile. Use
                        for high-volume topics where the default (deep=60)
                        under-covers. See issue #716.
  --max-per-source MAX_PER_SOURCE
                        Override the per-stream cap (per_stream_limit) applied
                        to each (source, subquery) before pooling. Raising it
                        increases unique-item yield when one source has many
                        relevant items. See issue #716.
  --max-source-fetches MAX_SOURCE_FETCHES
                        Override the per-source fetch cap (MAX_SOURCE_FETCHES,
                        default x=2) that limits how many subqueries actually
                        fetch a capped source. Raise it so every X subquery in
                        a multi-angle --plan runs instead of just the first
                        two. See issue #716.
  --auto-resolve        Use web search to discover subreddits/handles before
                        planning (for platforms without WebSearch)
  --github-user GITHUB_USER
                        GitHub username for person-mode search (e.g.,
                        steipete)
  --github-repo GITHUB_REPO
                        Comma-separated owner/repo for project-mode search
                        (e.g., openclaw/openclaw,paperclipai/paperclip)
  --trustpilot-domain TRUSTPILOT_DOMAIN
                        Trustpilot review-page domain for the topic (e.g.,
                        www.thriftbooks.com). Used verbatim, bypasses the
                        brand-shape gate, and auto-activates the opt-in
                        Trustpilot source for this run (unless
                        EXCLUDE_SOURCES=trustpilot). Find the domain with
                        `trustpilot-pp-cli search '<name>'`.
  --amazon-query AMAZON_QUERY
                        Product keyword the amazon source searches, when that
                        source is active. Defaults to the topic. Supply it
                        whenever the topic is not the product: a person topic
                        searches their company's product line (--amazon-
                        query='June Oven'), and a brand searches brand-plus-
                        category (--amazon-query='Weber grill', not 'Weber' --
                        a bare brand keyword lands on an ad-heavy page that
                        can miss the brand's own bestsellers). Requires the
                        brightdata CLI on PATH and logged in.
  --meta-ads-page META_ADS_PAGE
                        Meta Ad Library page id for the topic's advertiser,
                        when the meta_ads source is active. Skips name-based
                        page resolution and its discovery credit. Accepts a
                        bare numeric page id (e.g. 123456789012345) or an Ad
                        Library URL carrying view_all_page_id. A facebook.com
                        vanity URL is not a page id and is rejected. Use it
                        when a brand advertises under product names, or when
                        resolution picked the wrong company.
  --telegram-sources TELEGRAM_SOURCES
                        Comma-separated list of public Telegram channel
                        handles or t.me URLs. Auto-activates the opt-in
                        Telegram source for this run. Accepts: bare handle
                        (aipost), @handle (@aipost), t.me URL
                        (https://t.me/aipost), or preview URL
                        (https://t.me/s/aipost). Rejects joinchat links and
                        numeric -100 supergroup IDs.
  --competitors [N]     Auto-discover N competitor entities and fan out
                        last30days across all of them as a comparison (default
                        N=2 → 3-way: original + 2 peers; range 1..6). Use
                        --competitors-list to override discovery.
  --competitors-list COMPETITORS_LIST
                        Comma-separated competitor entities to skip discovery
                        (e.g., 'Anthropic,xAI,Google Gemini'). Implies
                        --competitors.
  --polymarket-keywords POLYMARKET_KEYWORDS
                        Comma-separated keywords that Polymarket market titles
                        must match to be included. Use for ambiguous single-
                        token topics like 'Warriors' (nba,gsw,golden-state) to
                        filter out Glasgow Warriors rugby, Honor of Kings
                        Rogue Warriors, etc. When omitted, Polymarket returns
                        all matching markets — so expect cross-entity noise on
                        generic topics.
  --competitors-plan COMPETITORS_PLAN
                        JSON mapping of per-entity Step 0.55 targeting for
                        competitor / vs-mode sub-runs. Schema: {entity_name:
                        {x_handle?, x_related?, subreddits?, github_user?,
                        github_repos?, context?}}. Accepts inline JSON or a
                        file path. Implies --competitors. Preferred over
                        --competitors-list when the hosting model has already
                        resolved per-entity handles and subs.
